#### Summary
Because `ComputeLastAccessiblePostTime` was returning a concrete error, when it returned the nil type, and other methods returned the error interface, the type was being wrapped up into the error interface, so even though the error interfaces *value* was nil, the type was not equal to `nil`. This is an instance of https://go.dev/doc/faq#nil_error . This resulted in the job execution reporting as in error, even though there was no error, and when trying to print the error, a panic occurred. The fix is to have  `ComputeLastAccessiblePostTime` return the error interface instead of the concrete error type.

As a bonus, I also fixed nil checking for license in case license exists but does not have features, and fixed the wrapping error message for the job failure execution path.

